ater & Burst Pipe Claim Appraisal","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/what-we-appraise/burst-pipe-water-claims/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Fire & Smoke Claim Appraisal","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/what-we-appraise/house-fire-smoke-claims/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Wildfire, Ember & Smoke Appraisal","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/what-we-appraise/wildfire-ember-claims/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Snow Load & Ice Dam Appraisal","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/what-we-appraise/snow-load-ice-dam-claims/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Insurance Estimate Review","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/what-we-appraise/carrier-estimate-second-look/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Umpire Services","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/what-we-appraise/neutral-umpire/"}}]},"description":"Independent insurance appraisal, estimate review and umpire services for disputed hail, wind, snow, water and fire claims in all 23 Wyoming counties.","areaServed":[{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"},{"@type":"City","name":"Cheyenne","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Casper","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Laramie","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Gillette","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Rock Springs","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Sheridan","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Green River","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Evanston","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Riverton","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Jackson","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Cody","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Rawlins","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Wyoming"}}],"priceRange":"$$","knowsAbout":["Insurance appraisal","Appraisal clause","Hail damage","Wind damage","Snow load","Xactimate estimating","Umpire services"],"openingHoursSpecification":[{"@type":"OpeningHoursSpecification","dayOfWeek":["Monday","Tuesday","Wednesday","Thursday","Friday"],"opens":"08:00","closes":"18:00"}]},{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/#website","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/","name":"Wyoming Insurance Appraiser","publisher":{"@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-answers/#webpage","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-answers/","name":"Insurance Appraisal FAQ for Wyoming | Answers by Topic","description":"Answers to common Wyoming insurance appraisal questions, grouped by topic: how it works, cost and timing, state rules and working with an appraiser.","inLanguage":"en-US","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/#website"},"about":{"@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"dateModified":"2026-11-11","primaryImageOfPage":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/team-meeting.webp","width":960,"height":640},"breadcrumb":{"@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-answers/#breadcrumb"},"mainEntity":{"@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-answers/#faq"}},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Appraisal answers","item":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-answers/"}],"@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-answers/#breadcrumb"},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is insurance appraisal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A process written into most property policies for settling disagreements about the amount of a covered loss. Each side names an appraiser, the appraisers choose an umpire, and an agreement signed by any two of the three sets the amount."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is appraisal the same as arbitration?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"They are similar but not identical. Appraisal is narrower: it decides the amount of loss, not legal questions such as coverage or bad faith, and it is usually less formal than arbitration."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who can demand appraisal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Under most policy wording, either you or the insurance company can demand it in writing once you disagree on the amount of loss."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does my policy have an appraisal clause?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most Wyoming homeowners, farm and commercial property policies do. Look for a paragraph titled “Appraisal” in the conditions section. Surplus lines and specialty policies sometimes use different wording or replace it with arbitration."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does appraisal cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You pay your own appraiser and usually half of the umpire’s fee. Appraiser fees may be flat, hourly or tied to the claim; ask for the arrangement in writing. Our award net-gain projector helps you see whether the cost makes sense."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does appraisal take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Many residential appraisals finish within two to three months after both appraisers are named. Winter access in the mountains, large commercial losses and umpire hearings can extend it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does appraisal stop the clock on my deadline to sue?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not automatically. Unless your policy or a written agreement says otherwise, the suit-limitation period may keep running. Protect it separately."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who regulates insurance companies in Wyoming?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Wyoming Department of Insurance, based in Cheyenne. It licenses insurers and adjusters and accepts consumer complaints."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Wyoming have a FAIR plan or wind pool?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Wyoming does not operate a FAIR plan or a state wind pool. Hard-to-insure properties are usually written in the surplus lines market."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Wyoming have a bad-faith law?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Wyoming recognizes a common-law claim for first-party bad faith, and its insurance code includes unfair claim practices rules and a provision on attorney’s fees and interest for unreasonable delays. Those are legal questions; ask a Wyoming attorney. Appraisal does not decide them."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many counties do you cover?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"All 23 Wyoming counties, from Laramie County in the southeast to Teton and Park counties in the northwest."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are you a public adjuster or a law firm?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Neither. We provide appraisal, estimate review and umpire services. We don’t negotiate claims outside appraisal and we don’t give legal advice."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you tell me if my claim is worth appraising?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The first conversation is free. We’ll look at both estimates and your photos and give you a straight answer — including when appraisal isn’t the right tool."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you guarantee a result?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No honest appraiser can. We guarantee a careful, well-documented valuation and clear communication."}}],"@id":"https://wyominginsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-answers/#faq"}]}</script>
