<section class="phero"><img class="phero-bg" src="/assets/img/photos/team-meeting.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/team-meeting-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/team-meeting.webp 960w" sizes="100vw" width="960" height="640" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-zoom><div class="wrap"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Appraisal answers</span></nav><p class="kicker">Answers</p><h1>Insurance Appraisal Questions, Answered for Wyoming</h1><p class="lede">Plain answers grouped by topic: appraisal basics, cost and timing, Wyoming specifics and working with us.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line-light" href="/talk-to-us/">Free claim review</a></div></div></section><div class="wrap twocol"><article class="prose"><div class="jump"><a href="#faq-0">Appraisal basics</a><a href="#faq-1">Cost and timing</a><a href="#faq-2">Wyoming specifics</a><a href="#faq-3">Working with us</a></div><h2 id="faq-0">Appraisal basics</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What is insurance appraisal?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>A process written into most property policies for settling disagreements about the amount of a covered loss. Each side names an appraiser, the appraisers choose an umpire, and an agreement signed by any two of the three sets the amount.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is appraisal the same as arbitration?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>They are similar but not identical. Appraisal is narrower: it decides the amount of loss, not legal questions such as coverage or bad faith, and it is usually less formal than arbitration.</p></div></details><details><summary>Who can demand appraisal?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Under most policy wording, either you or the insurance company can demand it in writing once you disagree on the amount of loss.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does my policy have an appraisal clause?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Most Wyoming homeowners, farm and commercial property policies do. Look for a paragraph titled “Appraisal” in the conditions section. Surplus lines and specialty policies sometimes use different wording or replace it with arbitration.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-1">Cost and timing</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>How much does appraisal cost?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>You pay your own appraiser and usually half of the umpire’s fee. Appraiser fees may be flat, hourly or tied to the claim; ask for the arrangement in writing. Our award net-gain projector helps you see whether the cost makes sense.</p></div></details><details><summary>How long does appraisal take?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Many residential appraisals finish within two to three months after both appraisers are named. Winter access in the mountains, large commercial losses and umpire hearings can extend it.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does appraisal stop the clock on my deadline to sue?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Not automatically. Unless your policy or a written agreement says otherwise, the suit-limitation period may keep running. Protect it separately.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-2">Wyoming specifics</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Who regulates insurance companies in Wyoming?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>The Wyoming Department of Insurance, based in Cheyenne. It licenses insurers and adjusters and accepts consumer complaints.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does Wyoming have a FAIR plan or wind pool?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. Wyoming does not operate a FAIR plan or a state wind pool. Hard-to-insure properties are usually written in the surplus lines market.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does Wyoming have a bad-faith law?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Wyoming recognizes a common-law claim for first-party bad faith, and its insurance code includes unfair claim practices rules and a provision on attorney’s fees and interest for unreasonable delays. Those are legal questions; ask a Wyoming attorney. Appraisal does not decide them.</p></div></details><details><summary>How many counties do you cover?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>All 23 Wyoming counties, from Laramie County in the southeast to Teton and Park counties in the northwest.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-3">Working with us</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Are you a public adjuster or a law firm?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Neither. We provide appraisal, estimate review and umpire services. We don’t negotiate claims outside appraisal and we don’t give legal advice.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can you tell me if my claim is worth appraising?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. The first conversation is free. We’ll look at both estimates and your photos and give you a straight answer — including when appraisal isn’t the right tool.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you guarantee a result?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No honest appraiser can. We guarantee a careful, well-documented valuation and clear communication.</p></div></details></div></article><aside class="side"><div class="side-box side-call"><p class="side-t">Talk it through</p><p>The first conversation is free. We’ll tell you honestly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="side-tel" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-block" href="/talk-to-us/">Send claim details</a></div><div class="side-box"><p class="side-t">Resources</p><ul class="side-list"><li><a href="/appraisal-step-by-step/">Appraisal step by step</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-answers/" aria-current="page">Appraisal answers (FAQ)</a></li><li><a href="/claim-terms/">Claim terms glossary</a></li><li><a href="/claim-guides/">Claim guides</a></li></ul></div></aside></div><section class="strip"><div class="wrap strip-in rv"><div><p class="strip-t">Didn’t see your question?</p><p>Call or email — we’re glad to talk it through.</p></div><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-dark" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line-light" href="/talk-to-us/">Email the estimate</a></div></div></section>
